{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>For the land that you are coming there</b> etc. You need to keep His commandments." "<b>For the land that you are coming there, it is not like the land of Egypt, where you would sow your seed</b> etc. Rather, what does it mean? You have need that HaShem set His eyes upon it continually; therefore, 'and it shall be, if you indeed hearken, I will give the rain of your land' etc." "<b>It is not like the land of Egypt</b> etc. Rashi explained: Ham built Zoan for Egypt, and Canaan built Hebron, and so forth. And what Rashi explained in the pericope of Lekh Lekha — 'and the Canaanite was then in the land' — that he was going and conquering the land of Israel from the seed of Shem — that is from the northern side of the land of Israel, which fell to the portion of Shem; but part of the south of the land of Israel fell to the portion of Canaan, and so Hebron was built, as he explains in the pericope of Lekh Lekha."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:27.001399540Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}